## What to deliver

Build and rig the foundry up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a squat armored bunker-forge with a broad blast
door set into its front and a great drive flywheel on its flank. **Author the two
required animations** as F-curves with the `voxel-anim` animation subcommands:
`blast_door_raise` (the heavy door easing up off its rest, holding open, then easing
back down and settling shut — a weighty portcullis cycle, not a constant-speed slide)
and `flywheel_spin` (the great wheel turning a full, steady revolution each loop with
no jerk at the loop seam). Both are self-playing idles that run continuously on their
own while the building body stays fixed. The animations are the fixed contract —
produce both, by those names; the parts and joints that realize them are yours. When
you are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished
submission.
